  "title": "Reducing Conflict Through Clear Communication",
  "content": "Many conflicts between parents and children come from unclear expectations or mixed messages. Children need simple, direct communication that matches their developmental level. When instructions are too long, too fast, or too emotional, children may become confused or overwhelmed.\n\nThis lesson teaches parents how to give clear, age‑appropriate instructions and how to check for understanding. Parents also learn how to avoid communication habits that escalate conflict, such as sarcasm, threats, or shouting.\n\nClear communication helps children know what is expected and reduces power struggles. It also helps parents stay calm and consistent.",
  "activities": [
    "Give one instruction today using ten words or fewer. Observe how your child responds.",
    "After giving an instruction, ask your child to repeat it back in their own words."
  ],
  "reflectionQuestions": [
    "What communication habits tend to escalate conflict in your home?",
    "How does your child respond when instructions are simple and clear?",
    "What changes can you make to reduce misunderstandings?"
